{
  "analysis": "Ah, let's examine why normal and exponential failed. In `ars()`: when calculating intersection points `z[i+1]`, for standard normal or exponential, tangents might intersect outside the valid region or parallel. Standard ARS implementation (Gilks & Wild 1992) defines intersection points $z_i$ of tangents at abscissae $x_i$ and $x_{i+1}$ as:
$z_0 = L$
$z_i = \frac{h(x_{i+1}) - h(x_i) - s_{i+1} x_{i+1} + s_i x_i}{s_i - s_{i+1}}$ for $i = 1, \dots, k-1$
